.TH MGNT 1 "October 31, 2026" "magenta" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mgnt \- color, page, follow, and search logs and command output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mgnt
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mgnt
reads logs or the output of commands, from files or standard input, and colors each line by what kind it is.
It detects the kind of input on its own.
It knows logs such as unicorn, cron, rails, nginx, JSON lines, and syslog, and the output of commands such as
.BR git (1),
.BR jj ,
.BR "go test" ,
.BR pytest ,
.BR terraform ,
.BR "docker build" ,
and
.BR "curl \-v" ,
and manual pages (\fBman ls | mgnt\fR).
.PP
When standard output is a terminal,
.B mgnt
also behaves like
.BR less (1).
Output that fits on the screen is printed.
A lot of output that is ready at once opens a full-screen pager that scrolls both ways.
A log that keeps growing, such as the output of
.BR "tail \-f" ,
streams into the terminal scrollback.
Press
.B /
in the pager or in a followed log to search with
.BR fzf (1)
while new lines keep arriving.
.PP
When the output is not a terminal, or with
.BR \-\-no\-interactive ,
.B mgnt
only colors.
.PP
Lines are never changed.
Removing the color codes from the output gives back the input, byte for byte.
Lines longer than 64 KiB pass through uncolored.
.PP
.B mgnt
shows logs and never changes any file.
To manage its rules, colorschemes, and settings, use
.BR magenta (1).
.SH OPTIONS
Options change a setting for one run only and never write
.IR config.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-ansi " strip" | keep
What to do with colors already in the input.
.B strip
replaces them with the colors of
.BR mgnt ,
and
.B keep
leaves the lines alone.
.TP
.BI \-\-buffer " lines"
The number of lines kept for the
.B /
search.
.TP
.BI \-\-colorscheme " name"
Use this colorscheme.
The names are listed by
.BR "magenta colorscheme list" .
.TP
.BI \-\-fzf\-opts " options"
Extra
.BR fzf (1)
options.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-interactive
Never open the pager or the fzf search.
Only color the input.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-preview
Do not show the preview pane in the
.B /
search.
.TP
.BI \-\-set " key" = value
Change any setting of
.IR config.toml ,
such as
.B \-\-set preview_window=right,40%
or
.BR \-\-set\ keys.accept=enter .
It can be repeated and is applied after the other options.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " auto" | dark | light
Use the dark or the light palette of the colorscheme.
.B auto
picks one by the background of the terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH PAGER KEYS
.TP
.BR j ", " Down ", " Enter
One line down.
.TP
.BR k ", " Up ", " y
One line up.
.TP
.BR Space ", " f ", " PageDown
One screen down.
.TP
.BR b ", " PageUp
One screen up.
.TP
.BR d " and " u
Half a screen down and up.
.TP
.BR g " and " G
The top and the end.
.TP
.B F
Follow: stay on the newest line as the input grows.
Any key stops it.
.TP
.B w
Chop long lines instead of wrapping them, and back.
.TP
.B #
Show line numbers.
.TP
.BR n " and " N
The next and the previous match of the last search.
.TP
.B /
Search with fzf.
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.PP
In the search,
.B Ctrl\-o
accepts: it jumps to the line in the pager, or prints the selected lines in a followed log.
.B Ctrl\-/
opens and closes the preview of the lines around a match, and
.B Esc
leaves.
Both keys can be changed in
.IR config.toml .
The preview pane needs
.BR fzf (1)
0.49.0 or newer.
Search without a preview works with older versions.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magenta/config.toml
The settings, or
.I ~/.config/magenta/config.toml
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
Read each time
.B mgnt
starts.
Change it with
.BR "magenta config set" .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magenta/rules/
Rules of the user.
A file with the same name as a built-in rule replaces it.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magenta/colorschemes/
Colorschemes of the user, with the same override behavior.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, no colors are written.
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
turns colors off.
Together with
.B COLORTERM
it also picks the color depth: truecolor, 256 colors, or 16 colors.
.TP
.B MGNT_FZF_OPTS
Extra
.BR fzf (1)
options, added after the
.B fzf_opts
setting.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the configuration directory is.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A file could not be read, or the output could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
The options or a setting are not valid.
Nothing was read.
.SH EXAMPLES
Follow a log:
.PP
.RS
.EX
tail \-f unicorn.log | mgnt
.EE
.RE
.PP
Color and page the output of a command:
.PP
.RS
.EX
git log \-p | mgnt
go test ./... 2>&1 | mgnt
.EE
.RE
.PP
Page a file, and pipe the colored text on:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mgnt app.log
mgnt app.log | less \-R
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use another colorscheme for one run:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mgnt \-\-colorscheme mono app.log
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR magenta (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR less (1)
.PP
Documentation and source: https://github.com/styd/magenta
